  "details": "I have hypermobile joints and when exploring worlds that require me to continuously press forwards on the joystick, my fingers can be stressed in a way that causes discomfort. I would still like to “move normally” without having to use teleport locomotion. Thus I think it would be an improvement for people with chronic joint pains (especially in the hands/fingers) to be able to control movements with a zero-g style input as we can float in an intended direction with minimal input. World creators could still limit with invisible walls where they do not intend for players to go.\n\nI imagine it would not be too much to enable in game universally? The feature I am describing already exists in many Space Jam worlds (from which I got the idea).\n\nThanks.\n\niPod",
